{"kind":"create","at":"2026-05-14T03:56:47.5335873+00:00","by":"nick-boey","issueId":"xqqoHb","data":{"id":"xqqoHb","title":"fleece migrate doesn\u0027t invalidate replay cache","description":"MigrationService.WriteSnapshotAsync (src/Fleece.Core/EventSourcing/Services/Legacy/MigrationService.cs:190) writes the snapshot directly via _fileSystem and never calls _replayCache.InvalidateAsync. If a stale .fleece/.replay-cache exists at the current HEAD SHA (e.g., from running \u0027fleece list\u0027 on the new event-sourced reader before \u0027fleece migrate\u0027 completes), the cache survives migration and EventSourcedStorageService.GetIssuesAsync (EventSourcedStorageService.cs:60) trusts it \u2014 \u0027fleece list\u0027 returns empty even though .fleece/issues.jsonl is populated.\n\nRepro: on a repo with legacy issue files, upgrade to 3.1.0, run \u0027fleece list\u0027 once (writes empty cache at HEAD), then \u0027fleece migrate\u0027, then \u0027fleece list\u0027 \u2014 shows \u0027No issues found\u0027. Workaround: delete .fleece/.replay-cache.\n\nFix: MigrationService should call IReplayCache.InvalidateAsync after writing the snapshot, matching EventSourcedStorageService.WriteSnapshotAsync:93-100.","status":"Open","type":"Bug","linkedIssues":[],"parentIssues":[],"tags":[],"executionMode":"Series","createdBy":"nick-boey","createdAt":"2026-05-14T03:56:47.5335873\u002B00:00","lastUpdate":"2026-05-14T03:56:47.5335873\u002B00:00"}}
